.TH SALLE 1 2026-11-04 garnish "garnish manual"
.SH NAME
salle \- create, edit, start and stop garnish VMs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B salle
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Salle
is a GTK application for the VMs that
.BR gerantd (1)
runs. It talks to
.B gerantd
over the session bus, and reads and writes the VMs' configuration files in
.I ~/.config/garnish/vms/
itself.
.TP
.B List
Every VM with a configuration file, with its state and a button to start
or shut it down. VMs started or stopped elsewhere, such as with
.BR gerant (1),
and files added, changed or removed in the directory show up too.
.TP
.B Start, Shut Down, Force Off
.BR StartVm ,
.B StopVm
(the ACPI power button) and, after asking,
.BR KillVm .
If a start fails, Salle shows gerantd's message with a way to the logs.
.TP
.B Running VMs
The ssh command, to copy or to open in a terminal through
.BR xdg\-terminal\-exec ,
the IPv4 and IPv6 addresses, tap device, vsock CID and crosvm's PID.
.TP
.B Sound
For a running VM with
.BR Audio=yes ,
a volume slider and a mute button for the VM's stream on the host.
.TP
.B Apps
For a VM with
.BR Wayland=yes ,
the guest's graphical applications, from the list
.BR carte (1)
keeps, also while the VM is off. Clicking one in a running VM opens it.
With
.BR AppMenu=yes ,
editing the VM chooses which ones are in the host's application menu.
.TP
.B New and Edit
One dialog for the common settings and, under Advanced, the kernel, initrd,
extra kernel parameters, GPU context types and extra crosvm arguments.
.TP
.B Delete
Removes the configuration file. The image and logs stay.
.TP
.B Logs
The VM's logs, followed as they grow.
.PP
Salle edits configuration files in place: changing a setting rewrites only
that setting's lines, so comments, other settings and their order stay.
Settings in drop-ins are shown, but saving only changes the main file, so a
drop-in still wins.
.SH OPTIONS
Salle takes the standard GTK application options; see
.BR "salle \-\-help\-all" .
.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B Ctrl+N
New VM.
.TP
.BR F5 ", " Ctrl+R
Refresh.
.TP
.B Ctrl+E
Edit the selected VM's settings.
.TP
.B Ctrl+L
Show its logs.
.TP
.B Ctrl+T
Open a terminal with ssh into it.
.TP
.B Ctrl+?
Keyboard shortcuts.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q
Quit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/garnish/vms/name.conf
VM configurations; see
.BR garnish\-vm.conf (5).
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/garnish/name/
VM logs.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/carte/apps/name.json
A VM's applications, written by
.BR carte (1).
.PP
Window size and the last selected VM are kept in GSettings, under
.BR org.garnish.Salle .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gerant (1),
.BR gerantd (1),
.BR garnish\-vm.conf (5),
.BR carte (1),
.BR garnish (7)
